AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CHEBI_32159 "Europe::955")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:CHEBI_32159 "sucralose (trichlorogalactosucrose)"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CHEBI_32159 "LanguaL term definition: Food additive; technological purpose(s): sweetener.


Sucralose is an artificial sweetener. The majority of ingested sucralose is not broken down by the body and therefore it is non-caloric. In the European Union, it is also known under the E number (additive code) E955. Sucralose is approximately 600 times as sweet as sucrose (table sugar), twice as sweet as saccharin, and 3 times as sweet as aspartame."@en)
SubClassOf(obo:CHEBI_32159 obo:FOODON_03412972)

