AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_00002531 "bull"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:FOODON_00002531 "A steer is a younger animal that may not be trained, or may not be strong and mature enough for hard work. In the United States a steer is not considered an ox until it is four years old, by which time it is considered large enough and mature enough for any work required of it.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_00002531 "cattle steer"@en)
