AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_00003079 "Dioscorea polystachya or Chinese yam is a species of flowering plant in the yam family.  It is a perennial climbing vine, native to China and East Asia.[3][4] The edible tubers are cultivated largely in Asia and sometimes used in alternative medicine. This species of yam is unique as the tubers can be eaten raw."@en)
