AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03411110 "The adzuki bean (*Vigna angularis* (English: red mung bean) is an annual vine widely grown throughout East Asia and the Himalayas for its small (approximately 5 mm) bean. The cultivars most familiar in Northeast Asia have a uniform red colour, however, white, black, gray, and variously mottled varieties also are known.[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adzuki_bean]"@en)
