# Class: obo:FOODON_03411129 (trout and salmon family)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03411129 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03411129 "Salmonidae is a family of ray-finned fish, the only living family currently placed in the order Salmoniformes. It includes salmon, trout, chars, freshwater whitefishes, and graylings, which collectively are known as the salmonids. The Atlantic salmon and trout of the genus *Salmo* give the family and order their names. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salmonidae]"@en)
