# Class: obo:FOODON_03411184 (temperate bass families)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03411184 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03411184 "The *Moronidae* are a family of perciform fishes, commonly called the temperate basses, consisting of at least six freshwater, brackish water, and marine species. The members of this family are most commonly found near the coastal regions of eastern North America (including the Gulf of Mexico), northern Africa, and Europe. The family includes the genera *Morone* and *Dicentrarchus*. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moronidae] 
The members of the family *Percichthyidae* are known as the temperate perches. They belong to the order Perciformes, the perch-like fishes. Almost 40 species of percichthyids are now recognised, grouped in 10 genera. Most but not all are exclusively freshwater fishes. They are mainly found in Australia, but species are also found in southern South America (Percichthys) and eastern Asia (Coreoperca and Siniperca).
[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Temperate_perch]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411184 <http://eol.org/pages/5184>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411184 langual:B1184)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03411184 "moronidae"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03411184 "percichthyidae"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03411184 "temperate bass families"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03411184 obo:FOODON_03411581)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03411185 (baby lima bean plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03411185 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03411185 "In the United Kingdom and the United States, \"butter beans\" refers to either dried beans which can be purchased to rehydrate, or the canned variety which are ready to use. In culinary use there, lima beans and butter beans are distinct, the latter being large and yellow, the former small and green. In areas where both are considered to be lima beans, the green variety may be labelled as \"baby\" (and less commonly \"junior\") limas. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lima_bean]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411185 <http://eol.org/pages/645300>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411185 obo:NCBITaxon_3884)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411185 <http://www.ars-grin.gov/cgi-bin/npgs/html/taxon.pl?27591>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411185 <http://www.itis.gov/servlet/SingleRpt/SingleRpt?search_topic=TSN&search_value=26850>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411185 langual:B1185)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411185 "MANSFELD:27587")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411185 "PLANTS:PHLU2")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym obo:FOODON_03411185 "Phaseolus lunatus L.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03411185 "baby lima bean plant"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03411185 obo:FOODON_03411397)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03411186 (cranberry bean plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03411186 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03411186 "Also known as borlotti bean in Italy, the cranberry bean has a large, knobby beige pod splotched with red. The beans inside are cream-colored with red streaks and have a delicious nutlike flavor. Cranberry beans must be shelled before cooking. Heat diminishes their beautiful red color. They're available fresh in the summer and dried throughout the year."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411186 langual:B1186)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:FOODON_03411186 "borlotti bean"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:FOODON_03411186 "shell bean"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:FOODON_03411186 "shellout"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03411186 "phaseolus vulgaris"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03411186 "cranberry bean plant"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03411186 obo:FOODON_03411061)

