AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03411303 "Salvia is the largest genus of plants in the mint family, *Lamiaceae*, with nearly 1000 species of shrubs, herbaceous perennials, and annuals. Within the *Lamiaceae, Salvia* is part of the tribe *Mentheae* within the subfamily *Nepetoideae*. It is one of several genera commonly referred to as sage, it includes the widely produced herb used in cooking, *Salvia officinalis* (common sage, or just \"sage\"). [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salvia]"@en)
