# Class: obo:FOODON_03411369 (kohlrabi plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03411369 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03411369 "Kohlrabi is a biennial vegetable, a low, stout cultivar of wild cabbage. It is the same species as cabbage, broccoli, cauliflower, kale, Brussels sprouts, collard greens, Savoy cabbage, and gai lan. It can be eaten raw or cooked. Edible preparations are made with both the stem and the leaves. Despite its common names, it is not the same species as turnip."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:FOODON_03411369 wikipedia:Kohlrabi)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411369 <http://eol.org/pages/4219>)
