# Class: obo:FOODON_03411416 (pistachio plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03411416 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03411416 "The pistachio, *Pistacia vera* in the *Anacardiaceae* family, is a small tree originally from Persia (Iran), which now can also be found in to regions of Syria, Lebanon, Turkey, Greece, Kyrgyzstan, Turkmenistan, India, Pakistan, Egypt, Sicily and possibly Afghanistan (especially in the provinces of Samangan and Badghis). The fruit is a drupe, containing an elongated seed, which is the edible portion. The seed, commonly thought of as a nut, is a culinary nut, not a botanical nut."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411416 <http://eol.org/pages/483483>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411416 <http://www.ars-grin.gov/cgi-bin/npgs/html/taxon.pl?28655>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411416 <http://www.itis.gov/servlet/SingleRpt/SingleRpt?search_topic=TSN&search_value=506470>)
