AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03411477 "A small, well-branched tree or shrub from the family Annonaceae that bears edible fruits called sugar-apples or sweetsops. It tolerates a tropical lowland climate better than its relatives Annona reticulata and Annona cherimola, helping make it the most widely cultivated of these species."@en)
