# Class: obo:FOODON_03411530 (kumquat plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03411530 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03411530 "Kumquats (or cumquats in Australian English) (*Citrus japonica*) are a group of small fruit-bearing trees in the flowering plant family Rutaceae. They were previously classified as forming the now historical genus *Fortunella*, or placed within *Citrus sensu lato*. The edible fruit closely resembles the orange (*Citrus sinensis*), but it is much smaller, being approximately the size and shape of a large olive. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kumquat]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411530 <http://eol.org/pages/4414>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411530 <http://www.itis.gov/servlet/SingleRpt/SingleRpt?search_topic=TSN&search_value=500284>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411530 langual:B1530)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411530 "PLANTS:FORTU")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym obo:FOODON_03411530 "Fortunella Swingle")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03411530 "fortunella spp."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03411530 "kumquat plant"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03411530 obo:FOODON_03411139)

