# Class: obo:FOODON_03411553 (hickory tree)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03411553 "Trees in the genus *Carya* are commonly known as hickory, derived from the Powhatan language of Virginia.Hickory nuts (*Carya*) and walnuts (*Juglans*) in the *Juglandaceae* family grow within an outer husk; these fruits are technically drupes or drupaceous nuts, and thus not true botanical nuts. \"Tryma\" is a specialized term for such nut-like drupes."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03411553 "carya spp."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03411553 "hickory tree"@en)
