# Class: obo:FOODON_03411588 (black gram bean plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03411588 obo:IAO_0000122)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03411588 "Vigna mungo, black gram, urad bean, minapa pappu, mungo bean or black matpe bean is a bean grown in the Indian subcontinent. At one time it was considered to belong to the same species as the mung bean. The product sold as *black lentil* is usually the whole urad bean, whereas the split bean (the interior being white) is called *white lentil*. It should not to be confused with the much smaller true black lentil (*Lens culinaris*)."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411588 <http://eol.org/pages/654940>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411588 <http://www.ars-grin.gov/cgi-bin/npgs/html/taxon.pl?41621>)
