# Class: obo:FOODON_03411590 (saigon cinnamon plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03411590 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03411590 "Saigon cinnamon (*Cinnamomum loureiroi*, also known as Vietnamese cinnamon or Vietnamese cassia) is an evergreen tree indigenous to mainland Southeast Asia. Despite its name, Saigon cinnamon is more closely related to cassia (*C. cassia*) than to cinnamon (*C. verum*, \"true cinnamon\", Ceylon cinnamon), though in the same genus as both. 
Saigon cinnamon is used primarily for its aromatic bark, which has a taste quite similar to that of *C. cassia*, but with a more pronounced and complex aroma. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saigon_cinnamon]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411590 <http://eol.org/pages/4308>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411590 <http://www.ars-grin.gov/cgi-bin/npgs/html/taxon.pl?10583>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411590 langual:B1590)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym obo:FOODON_03411590 "Cinnamomum loureiroi Nees")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03411590 "cassia, saigon"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03411590 "cinnamomum loureiroi"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03411590 "cinnamomum lourieri"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03411590 "saigon cinnamon plant"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03411590 obo:FOODON_03411472)

