# Class: obo:FOODON_03411598 (siluriform fish)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03411598 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03411598 "Catfish (or catfishes; order Siluriformes or Nematognathi) are a diverse group of ray-finned fish. Despite their name, not all catfish have prominent barbel. Members of the Siluriformes order are defined by features of the skull and swimbladder. Catfish are of considerable commercial importance; many of the larger species are farmed or fished for food. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catfish]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411598 <http://eol.org/pages/5083>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411598 langual:B1598)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03411598 "catfishes"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03411598 "silures"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03411598 "siluriform fish"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03411598 obo:FOODON_03411365)

