# Class: obo:FOODON_03411674 (nettle plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03411674 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03411674 "Stinging nettle or common nettle, *Urtica dioica*, is a herbaceous perennial flowering plant, native to Europe, Asia, northern Africa, and North America, and is the best-known member of the nettle genus *Urtica*. The plant has many hollow stinging hairs called trichomes on its leaves and stems, which act like hypodermic needles, injecting histamine and other chemicals that produce a stinging sensation when contacted by humans and other animals. The plant has a long history of use as a medicine and as a food source."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411674 <http://eol.org/pages/595063>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411674 <http://www.ars-grin.gov/cgi-bin/npgs/html/taxon.pl?40944>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411674 <http://www.itis.gov/servlet/SingleRpt/SingleRpt?search_topic=TSN&search_value=19152>)
