# Class: obo:FOODON_03411731 (nalta jute plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03411731 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03411731 "Jute is a long, soft, shiny vegetable fibre that can be spun into coarse, strong threads. It is produced from plants in the genus *Corchorus*, which has been classified in the family *Tiliaceae*, or more recently in *Malvaceae*. However, it has been reclassified within the family *Sparrmanniaceae*.
 Jute is one of the most affordable natural fibres and is second only to cotton in amount produced and variety of uses of vegetable fibres."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411731 <http://eol.org/pages/584868>)
