# Class: obo:FOODON_03411892 (sucker family)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03411892 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03411892 "The *Catostomidae* are the suckers of the order Cypriniformes, with about 78 species in this family of freshwater fishes. The *Catostomidae* are primarily native to North America, but *Catostomus catostomus* is found in both North America and Russia, and *Myxocyprinus asiaticus* is from China.. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catostomidae]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411892 <http://eol.org/pages/3196>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03411892 langual:B1892)
