# Class: obo:FOODON_03412056 (senna plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03412056 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03412056 "Senna , the sennas, is a large genus of flowering plants in the legume family *Fabaceae*, and the subfamily Caesalpinioideae. This diverse genus is native throughout the tropics, with a small number of species in temperate regions. The number of species is estimated to be from about 260 to 350. The type species for the genus is Senna alexandrina. About 50 species of Senna are known in cultivation. 
 Cassia gum, an extract of the seeds of Chinese senna (*S. obtusifolia*), is used as a thickening agent. The leaves and flowers of Siamese cassia (*S. siamea *) are used in some Southeast Asian cuisines, such as Thai and Lao cuisines. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Senna_(plant)]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03412056 <http://eol.org/pages/4277>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03412056 <http://www.ars-grin.gov/cgi-bin/npgs/html/taxon.pl?310662>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03412056 langual:B2056)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03412056 "PLANTS:SENNA")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym obo:FOODON_03412056 "Senna")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym obo:FOODON_03412056 "Senna Mill.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym obo:FOODON_03412056 "Senna spp.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03412056 "cassia spp."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03412056 "senna spp."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03412056 "senna plant"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03412056 obo:FOODON_03411179)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03412057 (rooibos plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03412057 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03412057 "Rooibos, \"red bush\"; scientific name *Aspalathus linearis* is a broom-like member of the legume family of plants growing in South Africa's fynbos.
 
The generic name comes from the plant Calicotome villosa, aspalathos in Greek. This plant has very similar growth and flowers to the redbush. The specific name linearis comes from the plant's linear growing structure and needle-like leaves.

 The plant is used to make a herbal tea called rooibos tea, bush tea (esp. Southern Africa), redbush tea (esp. UK), South African red tea, or red tea. The product has been popular in Southern Africa for generations and is now consumed in many countries. It is sometimes spelled rooibosch in accordance with the old Dutch etymology."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03412057 <http://eol.org/pages/4277>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03412057 <http://www.ars-grin.gov/cgi-bin/npgs/html/taxon.pl?310979>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03412057 <http://www.itis.gov/servlet/SingleRpt/SingleRpt?search_topic=TSN&search_value=506239>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03412057 langual:B2057)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03412057 "PLANTS:ASLI14")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:FOODON_03412057 "rooibos")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03412057 "aspalathus linearis"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03412057 "rooibos plant"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03412057 obo:FOODON_03411179)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03412057 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_155124))

