# Class: obo:FOODON_03412111 (gastropod)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03412111 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03412111 "The Gastropoda or gastropods, more commonly known as snails and slugs, are a large taxonomic class within the phylum Mollusca. Gastropoda (previously known as univalves and sometimes spelled \"Gasteropoda\") are a major part of the phylum Mollusca, and are the most highly diversified class in the phylum, with 65,000 to 80,000 living snail and slug species. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gastropoda] 
The taxonomic class *Gastropoda* also includes snails that live in different habitats, such as land snails, marine and freshwater snails.."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03412111 <http://eol.org/pages/2366>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03412111 langual:B2111)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03412111 "gastropoda"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03412111 "gastropod"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03412111 obo:FOODON_00005706)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03412111 obo:FOODON_03412112)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03412112 (mollusc)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03412112 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03412112 "Mollusca is a large phylum of invertebrate animals whose members are known as molluscs or mollusks. Molluscs are the largest marine phylum, comprising about 23% of all the named marine organisms. Numerous molluscs also live in freshwater and terrestrial habitats. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mollusca]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03412112 <http://eol.org/pages/2195>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03412112 langual:B2112)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03412112 asfis:mol)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03412112 "EC:No 216/2009 MOL")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:FOODON_03412112 "Mollusca")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:FOODON_03412112 "mollusk"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03412112 "mollusc"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03412112 obo:FOODON_03411433)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03412113 (bivalve)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03412113 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03412113 "Bivalvia, in previous centuries referred to as the *Lamellibranchiata* and *Pelecypoda*, is a class of marine and freshwater molluscs that have laterally compressed bodies enclosed by a shell consisting of two hinged parts. Bivalves as a group have no head and they lack some usual molluscan organs like the radula and the odontophore. They include the clams, oysters, cockles, mussels, scallops, and numerous other families that live in saltwater, as well as a number of families that live in freshwater.[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bivalvia]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03412113 <http://eol.org/pages/2215>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03412113 langual:B2113)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03412113 "bivalvia"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03412113 "lamellibranchiata"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03412113 "pelecypod"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03412113 "pelecypoda"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03412113 "bivalve"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03412113 obo:FOODON_00005705)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03412113 obo:FOODON_03412112)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03412114 (snail)

AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03412114 langual:B2114)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:FOODON_03412114 "Snail is a common name loosely applied to shelled gastropods ... members of the molluscan class *Gastropoda* that have a coiled shell that is large enough for the animal to retract completely into. Gastropods that naturally lack a shell, or have only an internal shell, are mostly called slugs, and land snails that have only a very small shell (that they cannot retract into) are often called semi-slugs. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snail]"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03412114 obo:FOODON_00002244)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03412115 (echinoderm)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03412115 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03412115 "Echinoderm is the common name given to any member of the phylum *Echinodermata* of marine animals. The adults are recognizable by their (usually five-point) radial symmetry, and include such well-known animals as sea stars, sea urchins, sand dollars, and sea cucumbers, as well as the sea lilies or \"stone lilies\". [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Echinoderm]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03412115 langual:B2115)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03412115 asfis:ech)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03412115 "EC:No 1637/2001 ECH")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym obo:FOODON_03412115 "Echinodermata")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym obo:FOODON_03412115 "Echinodermata Klein, 1734")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03412115 "echinodermata"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03412115 "echinoderm"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03412115 obo:FOODON_00005703)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03412115 obo:FOODON_03411433)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03412116 (cephalopod)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03412116 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03412116 "A cephalopod is any member of the molluscan class *Cephalopoda* such as a squid, octopus or nautilus. These exclusively marine animals are characterized by bilateral body symmetry, a prominent head, and a set of arms or tentacles modified from the primitive molluscan foot. Fishermen sometimes call them inkfish, referring to their common ability to squirt ink. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cephalopod]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03412116 <http://eol.org/pages/2312>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03412116 langual:B2116)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03412116 "cephalopoda"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03412116 "cephalopod"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03412116 obo:FOODON_00005707)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03412116 obo:FOODON_03412112)

