# Class: obo:FOODON_03412508 (spaghetti squash plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03412508 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03412508 "The spaghetti squash (*Cucurbita pepo* var. *fastigata*) (also called vegetable spaghetti, noodle squash, vegetable marrow, spaghetti marrow, and squaghetti) is an oblong seed-bearing variety of winter squash. The fruit can range either from ivory to yellow or orange in color. The orange varieties have a higher carotene content. Its center contains many large seeds. Its flesh is bright yellow or orange. When raw, the flesh is solid and similar to other raw squash; when cooked, the flesh falls away from the fruit in ribbons or strands like spaghetti."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:FOODON_03412508 "WIKIPEDIA:Spaghetti_squash")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03412508 langual:B2508)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03412508 "cucurbita pepo var. fastigata"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03412508 "vegetable spaghetti"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03412508 "spaghetti squash plant"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03412508 obo:FOODON_03411190)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03412509 (butternut squash plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03412509 obo:IAO_0000122)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03412509 "A type of winter squash that grows on a vine. It has a sweet, nutty taste similar to that of a pumpkin. It has tan-yellow skin and orange fleshy pulp with a compartment of seeds in the bottom. When ripe, it turns increasingly deep orange, and becomes sweeter and richer."@en)
