# Class: obo:FOODON_03412515 (ajowan plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03412515 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03412515 "Ajwain, ajowan *Trachyspermum ammi*, also known as Ajowan caraway, Oomam in Tamil, bishop's weed or carom, is an annual herb in the family *Apiaceae*. It originated in India. Both the leaves and the fruit (often mistakenly called seeds) of the plant are consumed by humans. The plant is also called bishop's weed, but this is a common name it shares with some other different plants. The \"seed\" (i.e., the fruit) is often confused with lovage \"seed\".[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ajwain]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03412515 <http://eol.org/pages/477954>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03412515 <http://www.ars-grin.gov/cgi-bin/npgs/html/taxon.pl?36803>)
