# Class: obo:FOODON_03412560 (pasilla pepper plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03412560 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03412560 "The pasilla chile or chile negro is the dried form of the chilaca chili pepper, a long and narrow member of species *Capsicum annuum*. In the United States, producers and grocers often incorrectly use \"pasilla\" to describe the poblano, a different, wider variety of pepper, the dried form of which is called an ancho. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pasilla]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03412560 langual:B2560)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03412560 "chilaca chili pepper"@en)
