# Class: obo:FOODON_03412793 (bitterwood plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03412793 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03412793 "Quassia amara is a species in the genus *Quassia*, with some botanists treating it as the sole species in the genus. It is famous and used for the bitterwood or quassia, its heartwood, used as a febrifuge; this contains quassin, a bitter-tasting substance (it is, in fact, the bitterest substance found in nature). Extracts of *Q. amara* bark containing quassinoids are used as insecticides, being particularly useful against aphids on crop plants. It is also used to flavor aperitifs and bitters which are added to cocktails."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03412793 <http://eol.org/pages/582215>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03412793 <http://www.ars-grin.gov/cgi-bin/npgs/html/taxon.pl?30632>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03412793 <http://www.itis.gov/servlet/SingleRpt/SingleRpt?search_topic=TSN&search_value=28841>)
