# Class: obo:FOODON_03412953 (lemon verbena plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03412953 obo:IAO_0000122)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03412953 "Aloysia citrodora is a species of flowering plant in the verbena family *Verbenaceae*, native to Argentina, Paraguay, Brazil, Uruguay, Chile, Bolivia, and Peru. Common names include lemon verbena and lemon beebrush. It was brought to Europe by the Spanish and the Portuguese in the 17th century.

Lemon verbena leaves are used to add a lemon flavor to fish and poultry dishes, vegetable marinades, salad dressings, jams, puddings, greek yogurt and beverages. It also is used to make herbal teas, or added to standard tea in place of actual lemon (as is common with Moroccan tea). It can also be used to make a sorbet. In addition, it has anti-Candida albicans activity. In the European Union, Verbena essential oils (Lippia citriodora Kunth.) and derivatives other than absolute are prohibited when used as a fragrance ingredient (Commission Directive 2009/164/EU of 22 December 2009)."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:FOODON_03412953 "WIKIPEDIA:Lemon_verbena")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03412953 <http://eol.org/pages/4304>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03412953 <http://www.ars-grin.gov/cgi-bin/npgs/html/taxon.pl?317750>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03412953 langual:B2953)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03412953 "MANSFELD:4474")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:FOODON_03412953 "lemon verbena"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym obo:FOODON_03412953 "Aloysia citrodora Palau")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03412953 "aloysia citrodora"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03412953 "lemon beebush"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03412953 "lippia triphylla"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03412953 "lemon verbena plant"@en)
