# Class: obo:FOODON_03413396 (yam plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03413396 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03413396 "Yam is the common name for some plant species in the genus *Dioscorea* (family *Dioscoreaceae*) that form edible tubers. Yams are perennial herbaceous vines cultivated for the consumption of their starchy tubers in many temperate and subtropical world regions. The tubers themselves are also called \"yams\", having numerous cultivars.

In parts of the United States and Canada, \"yam\" is sometimes used to refer to varieties of the completely unrelated sweet potato (*Ipomoea batatas*).[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yam_(vegetable)]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03413396 <http://eol.org/pages/8214>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03413396 <http://www.ars-grin.gov/cgi-bin/npgs/html/taxon.pl?300191>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03413396 langual:B3396)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym obo:FOODON_03413396 "Dioscorea L.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03413396 "dioscorea spp."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03413396 "dioscoreaceae"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03413396 "yam plant"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03413396 obo:FOODON_03411018)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03413400 (jack-bean plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03413400 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03413400 "Canavalia ensiformis, or (common) jack bean, is a legume which is used for animal fodder and human nutrition, especially in Brazil where it is called feijão-de-porco (\"pig bean\"). It is also the source of concanavalin A.[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canavalia_ensiformis]"@en)
