AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03413402 "Phaseolus acutifolius, the Tepary bean, is native to the southwestern United States and Mexico and has been grown there by the native peoples since pre-Columbian times. It is more drought-resistant than the common bean (*Phaseolus vulgaris*) and is grown in desert and semi-desert conditions from Arizona through Mexico to Costa Rica.[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phaseolus_acutifolius]"@en)
