# Class: obo:FOODON_03413411 (chinese box thorn plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03413411 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03413411 "Lycium chinense varietal of Wolfberry, commercially called goji berry, is the common name for the fruit of two very closely related species: *Lycium barbarum* and *Lycium chinense*, two species of boxthorn in the family *Solanaceae* (which also includes the potato, tomato, eggplant, deadly nightshade, chili pepper, and tobacco). It is native to southeastern Europe and Asia."@en)
