# Class: obo:FOODON_03413428 (marigold plant (Calendula))

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03413428 obo:IAO_0000122)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03413428 "Calendula officinalis, the pot marigold, ruddles, common marigold or Scotch marigold, is a plant in the genus *Calendula* of the family *Asteraceae*. Pot marigold florets are edible. They are often used to add color to salads or added to dishes as a garnish and in lieu of saffron. The leaves are edible but are often not palatable. They have a history of use as a potherb and in salads."@en)
