# Class: obo:FOODON_03413434 (snake gourd plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03413434 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03413434 "Trichosanthes cucumerina is a tropical or subtropical vine; its variety *T. cucumerina* var. *anguina* raised for its strikingly long fruit, in Asia eaten immature as a vegetable much like the summer squash, and in Africa, the reddish pulp of its mature fruit is used as an economical substitute of tomato. Common names of the cultivated variety include snake gourd, serpent gourd [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trichosanthes_cucumerina]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03413434 <http://eol.org/pages/595306>)
