# Class: obo:FOODON_03413453 (noble crayfish)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03413453 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03413453 "Astacus astacus, the European crayfish, noble crayfish or broad-fingered crayfish, is the most common species of crayfish in Europe. Like other crayfish, The European crayfish is restricted to freshwater, living only in unpolluted streams, rivers and lakes. It is found from France throughout central Europe, to the Balkan peninsula, and north as far as parts of the British Isles, Scandinavia, and the western parts of the former Soviet Union. 
*Astacus astacus* is susceptible to the crayfish plague carried by the invasive American species *Pacifastacus leniusculus*, and is therefore listed as \"vulnerable\" by the IUCN Red List of Threatened Species. Citation: Sket, B. 1996. Astacus astacus. 
In: IUCN 2006. 2006 IUCN Red List of Threatened Species. <www.iucnredlist.org>. Downloaded on 26 January 2007."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03413453 <http://eol.org/pages/1021866>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03413453 <http://www.itis.gov/servlet/SingleRpt/SingleRpt?search_topic=TSN&search_value=97333>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03413453 langual:B3453)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03413453 asfis:aas)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03413453 "CEC1993:1263")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:FOODON_03413453 "broad-fingered crayfish")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03413453 "astacus astacus"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03413453 "braod-fingered crayfish"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03413453 "european crayfish"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03413453 "noble crayfish"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03413453 obo:FOODON_03414139)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03413453 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_6715))

# Class: obo:FOODON_03413454 (danube crayfish)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03413454 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03413454 "Astacus leptodactylus, the Danube crayfish or Galician crayfish, is a species of crayfish native to eastern Europe. It can be distinguished most easily from the commoner European or broad-fingered crayfish (*Astacus astacus*) by the relatively thinner \"fingers\" of the claws."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:FOODON_03413454 "WIKIPEDIA:Astacus_leptodactylus")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03413454 langual:B3454)
