# Class: obo:FOODON_03413463 (edible frog)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03413463 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03413463 "The edible frog (*Pelophylax kl. esculentus*)  is a name for a common European frog, also known as the common water frog or green frog (however, this latter term is also used for the North American species Rana clamitans). It is used for food, particularly in France for the delicacy frog legs. *Pelophylax kl. esculentus* is the fertile hybrid of the pool frog (*Pelophylax lessonae*) and the marsh frog (*Pelophylax ridibundus*)."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:FOODON_03413463 wikipedia:Edible_frog)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03413463 <http://eol.org/pages/320013>)
