# Class: obo:FOODON_03413721 (sweet onion plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03413721 "Sweet onion is a variety of onion that is not pungent. There are several varieties of sweet onion. The term sweet onion comes from the perceived sweetness of the onion compared to other varieties. This perceived sweetness is derived from a low sulfur content and and high water content when compared to other onion varieties."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:FOODON_03413721 wikipedia:Sweet_onion)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03413721 langual:B3721)
