# Class: obo:FOODON_03414026 (cutlassfish family)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414026 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414026 "The cutlassfishes are about 40 species of predatory fish in the family *Trichiuridae* (order Perciformes) found in seas throughout the world. Fish of this family are long, slender, and generally steely blue or silver in colour, giving rise to their name. They have reduced or absent pelvic and caudal fins, giving them an eel-like appearance, and large fang-like teeth. Some of the species are known as scabbardfishes or hairtails; others are called frostfishes because they appear in late autumn and early winter, around the time of the first frosts."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:FOODON_03414026 wikipedia:Cutlassfish)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414026 <http://eol.org/pages/5194>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414026 langual:B4026)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414026 "hairtail"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414026 "trichiuridae"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03414026 "cutlassfish family"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03414026 obo:FOODON_03411581)

