# Class: obo:FOODON_03414292 (puffin)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414292 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414292 "Puffins are any of three small species of auk (or alcids) in the bird genus *Fratercula* with a brightly coloured beak during the breeding season. These are pelagic seabirds that feed primarily by diving in the water. They breed in large colonies on coastal cliffs or offshore islands, nesting in crevices among rocks or in burrows in the soil. Two species, the Tufted Puffin and Horned Puffin, are found in the North Pacific Ocean, while the Atlantic Puffin is found in the North Atlantic Ocean."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:FOODON_03414292 "WIKIPEDIA:Puffin")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414292 <http://eol.org/pages/84465>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414292 langual:B4292)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414292 "fratercula"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03414292 "puffin"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03414292 obo:FOODON_00002616)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03414293 (tufted puffin)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414293 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414293 "The Tufted Puffin (*Fratercula cirrhata*) also known as Crested Puffin, is a relatively abundant medium-sized pelagic seabird in the auk (*Alcidae*) family found throughout the North Pacific Ocean. It is one of three species of puffin that make up the *Fratercula* genus and is easily recognizable by its thick red bill and yellow tufts."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414293 <http://eol.org/pages/1049982>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414293 <http://www.itis.gov/servlet/SingleRpt/SingleRpt?search_topic=TSN&search_value=177032>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414293 langual:B4293)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414293 "crested puffin"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414293 "fratercula cirrhata"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03414293 "tufted puffin"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03414293 obo:FOODON_03414292)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03414293 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_43311))

# Class: obo:FOODON_03414294 (atlantic puffin)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414294 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414294 "The Atlantic Puffin (*Fratercula arctica*) is a seabird species in the auk family. It is a pelagic bird that feeds primarily by diving for fish, but also eats other sea creatures, such as squid and crustaceans. Its most obvious characteristic during the breeding season is its brightly coloured bill. Also known as the Common Puffin, it is the only puffin species which is found in the Atlantic Ocean. The curious appearance of the bird, with its large colourful bill and its striking piebald plumage, has given rise to nicknames such as '\"clown of the ocean\" and \"sea parrot\"."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414294 <http://eol.org/pages/1049938>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414294 <http://www.itis.gov/servlet/SingleRpt/SingleRpt?search_topic=TSN&search_value=177025>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414294 langual:B4294)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414294 "fratercula arctica"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03414294 "atlantic puffin"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03414294 obo:FOODON_03414292)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03414294 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_28701))

# Class: obo:FOODON_03414295 (horned puffin)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414295 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414295 "The Horned Puffin (*Fratercula corniculata*) is an auk, similar in appearance to the Atlantic Puffin; this bird's bill is yellow at the base and red at the tip. It is a pelagic seabird that feeds primarily by diving for fish. It nests in colonies, often with other auks."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414295 <http://eol.org/pages/1049960>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414295 <http://www.itis.gov/servlet/SingleRpt/SingleRpt?search_topic=TSN&search_value=177029>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414295 langual:B4295)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414295 "fratercula corniculata"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03414295 "horned puffin"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03414295 obo:FOODON_03414292)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03414295 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_28702))

# Class: obo:FOODON_03414296 (shearwater)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414296 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414296 "Shearwaters are medium-sized long-winged seabirds. There are more than 30 species of shearwaters, a few larger ones in the genus *Calonectris* and many smaller species in the genus *Puffinus*."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:FOODON_03414296 "WIKIPEDIA:Shearwater")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414296 <http://eol.org/pages/19902>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414296 langual:B4296)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414296 "calonectris"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414296 "puffinus"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03414296 "shearwater"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03414296 obo:FOODON_00002616)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03414297 (sooty shearwater)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414297 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414297 "The Sooty Shearwater (*Puffinus griseus*) is a medium-large shearwater in the seabird family *Procellariidae*. In New Zealand it is also known by its Maori name titi and as \"muttonbird\", like its relatives the Wedge-tailed Shearwater *(P. pacificus*) and the Australian Short-tailed Shearwater (*P. tenuirostris*)."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414297 <http://eol.org/pages/1047364>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414297 <http://www.itis.gov/servlet/SingleRpt/SingleRpt?search_topic=TSN&search_value=174553>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414297 langual:B4297)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414297 asfis:pfg)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414297 "muttonbird"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414297 "puffinus griseus"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414297 "titi"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03414297 "sooty shearwater"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03414297 obo:FOODON_03414296)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03414297 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_37052))

# Class: obo:FOODON_03414298 (elmleaf blackberry plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414298 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414298 "Rubus ulmifolius is a species of wild blackberry known by the English common name elmleaf blackberry or thornless blackberry and the Spanish common name zarzamora. It is native to Europe and North Africa, and it is widely known elsewhere as an introduced species and sometimes a noxious weed. It is a brambly shrub with compound leaves and small, white or pink flowers. The fruit is a blackberry."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414298 <http://eol.org/pages/625649>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414298 <http://www.ars-grin.gov/cgi-bin/npgs/html/taxon.pl?313548>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414298 <http://www.itis.gov/servlet/SingleRpt/SingleRpt?search_topic=TSN&search_value=504890>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414298 langual:B4298)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414298 "PLANTS:RUUL")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414298 "rubus ulmifolius"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414298 "thornless blackberry"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414298 "zarzamora"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03414298 "elmleaf blackberry plant"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03414298 obo:FOODON_03414206)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03414298 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_75099))

# Class: obo:FOODON_03414299 (spinu sowthistle plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414299 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414299 "Sonchus asper (Sharp-fringed Sow Thistle, Prickly Sow Thistle, Spiny Sow Thistle, or Spiny-leaved Sow Thistle) is an annual plant with spiny leaves and yellow flowers resembling those of the dandelion. The leaves are bluish-green, simple, lanceolate, with wavy and sometimes lobed margins, covered in spines on both the margins and beneath. The base of the leaf surrounds the stem. The plant can reach 180 cm (6 ft) in height. The leaves and stems emit a milky sap when cut. The flowers grow in clusters and the end of the stems.
This plant is native to Europe, but is also a common weed in North American roadsides, landscapes, and pastures. Its edible leaves make a palatable and nutritious leaf vegetable."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414299 <http://eol.org/pages/492388>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414299 <http://www.ars-grin.gov/cgi-bin/npgs/html/taxon.pl?34933>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414299 <http://www.itis.gov/servlet/SingleRpt/SingleRpt?search_topic=TSN&search_value=38424>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414299 langual:B4299)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414299 "PLANTS:SOAS")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:FOODON_03414299 "prickly sow-thistle")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414299 "prickly sow thistle"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414299 "rough sow thistle"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414299 "sharp-fringed sow thistle"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414299 "sonchus asper"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414299 "spiny leaved sow thistle"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414299 "spiny-leaf sow thistle"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414299 "spiny-leaf sowthistle"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03414299 "spinu sowthistle plant"@en)
