# Class: obo:FOODON_03414350 (cubeb plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414350 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414350 "Cubeb (*Piper cubeba*), or tailed pepper, is a plant in genus *Piper, cultivated for its fruit and essential oil. It is mostly grown in Java and Sumatra, hence sometimes called Java pepper. The fruits are gathered before they are ripe, and carefully dried. Commercial cubebs consist of the dried berries, similar in appearance to black pepper, but with stalks attached - the \"tails\" in \"tailed pepper\"."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414350 <http://eol.org/pages/491342>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414350 <http://www.ars-grin.gov/cgi-bin/npgs/html/taxon.pl?28578>)
