# Class: obo:FOODON_03414455 (stevia plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414455 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414455 "Stevia is a genus of about 240 species of herbs and shrubs in the sunflower family (Asteraceae), native to subtropical and tropical regions from western North America to South America. The species *Stevia rebaudiana*, commonly known as sweetleaf, sweet leaf, sugarleaf, or simply stevia, is widely grown for its sweet leaves. As a sweetener and sugar substitute, stevia's taste has a slower onset and longer duration than that of sugar, although some of its extracts may have a bitter or licorice-like aftertaste at high concentrations.
With its steviol glycoside extracts having up to 300 times the sweetness of sugar, stevia has garnered attention with the rise in demand for low-carbohydrate, low-sugar food alternatives."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414455 <http://eol.org/pages/483967>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414455 <http://www.ars-grin.gov/cgi-bin/npgs/html/taxon.pl?35581>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414455 <http://www.itis.gov/servlet/SingleRpt/SingleRpt?search_topic=TSN&search_value=505914>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414455 langual:B4455)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414455 "PLANTS:STRE2")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414455 "candyleaf"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414455 "stevia rebaudiana"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414455 "sugarleaf"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414455 "sweet leaf"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414455 "sweetleaf"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03414455 "stevia plant"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03414455 obo:FOODON_03411013)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03414455 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_55670))

