# Class: obo:FOODON_03414558 (lesser rhea)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414558 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414558 "Darwin's rhea (*Rhea pennata*), also known as the lesser rhea, is a large flightless bird, but the smaller of the two extant species of rheas. It is found in the Altiplano and Patagonia in South America."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414558 <http://eol.org/pages/130164>)
