# Class: obo:FOODON_03414559 (osteoglossiform fish)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414559 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414559 "Osteoglossiformes (Greek: \"bony tongues\") is a relatively primitive order of ray-finned fish that contains two sub-orders, the *Osteoglossoidei* and the *Notopteroidei*. All of at least 245 living species inhabit freshwater. They are found in South America, Africa, Australia and southern Asia, having first evolved in Gondwana before that continent broke up. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Osteoglossiformes]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414559 <http://eol.org/pages/5386>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414559 langual:B4559)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414559 "bonytongues"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414559 "osteoglossiformes"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03414559 "osteoglossiform fish"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03414559 obo:FOODON_03411365)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03414560 (mooneye family)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414560 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414560 "The mooneyes are a family, the *Hiodontidae*, of ray-finned fish comprising two living and three extinct species in the genus *Hiodon*. They are large-eyed, fork-tailed fish that physically resemble shads. Their common name comes from the metallic gold or silver shine of their eyes. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mooneye]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414560 <http://eol.org/pages/5386>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414560 langual:B4560)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414560 "hiodontidae"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414560 "mooneye"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03414560 "mooneye family"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03414560 obo:FOODON_03414559)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03414561 (goldeye)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414561 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414561 "The goldeye, *Hiodon alosoides*, is a species of fish in the mooneye family (Hiodontidae). It occurs from as far down the Mackenzie River as Aklavik in the north to Mississippi in the south, and from Alberta in the west to Ohio south of the Great Lakes, with an isolated population south of James Bay. It is notable for a conspicuous golden iris in the eyes."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414561 <http://eol.org/pages/994821>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414561 langual:B4561)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414561 "itis:161905")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03414561 "laquaiche aux yeux d'or"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03414561 "goldeye"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03414561 obo:FOODON_03414560)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03414561 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_54904))

# Class: obo:FOODON_03414562 (muskox)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414562 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414562 "The muskox (*Ovibos moschatus*, also spelled musk ox and musk-ox) is an Arctic mammal of the family Bovidae, noted for its thick coat and for the strong odor emitted during the seasonal rut by males, from which its name derives."@en)
