AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414609 "Saccharina latissima is a brown algae (class *Phaeophyceae*), of the family *Laminariaceae*. It is also known by the common names sea belt and Devil's apron, due to its shape. It is found in the north east Atlantic Ocean and the Barents Sea south to Galicia in Spain. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saccharina_latissima]"@en)
