# Class: obo:FOODON_03414611 (tub gurnard)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414611 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414611 "The tub gurnard, *Chelidonichthys lucerna* (also C. lucernus, Trigla lucerna, T. corax) is a species of bottom-dwelling coastal fish with a spiny armored head and fingerlike pectoral fins used for crawling along the sea bottom. The tub gurnard is a reddish fish with blue pectoral fins.  [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tub_gurnard]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414611 <http://eol.org/pages/221983>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414611 langual:B4611)
