# Class: obo:FOODON_03414669 (fetid passionflower)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414669 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414669 "Passiflora foetida (common names: wild maracuja, bush passion fruit, marya-marya, wild water lemon, stinking passionflower, love-in-a-mist or running pop) is a species of passion flower that is native to the southwestern United States, Mexico, the Caribbean, Central America, and much of South America. It has been introduced to tropical regions around the world, such as Southeast Asia and Hawaii. It is a creeping vine like other members of the genus, and yields an edible fruit. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Passiflora_foetida]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414669 <http://eol.org/pages/584516>)
