# Class: obo:FOODON_03414681 (australian millet plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414681 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414681 "Panicum decompositum, known by the common names native millet, Australian millet, papa grass, and umbrella grass, is a species of grass native to the inland of Australia. Native millet is a staple food of outback Aborigines, who hand-harvest the seed to make damper, a traditional soda bread. Farmers also highly prize the grass as pasture for stock. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Panicum_decompositum]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414681 <http://eol.org/pages/8223>)
