# Class: obo:FOODON_03414937 (spine gourd plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414937 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414937 "Momordica dioica, Bristly Balsam Pear, commonly known as spiny gourd or spine gourd and also known as prickly carolaho, Teasle gourd, kantola, is a species of flowering plant in the gourd family. It is used as a vegetable in all regions of India and some parts in South Asia. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Momordica_dioica]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414937 <http://eol.org/pages/483973>)
