# Class: obo:FOODON_03414957 (native currant plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414957 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414957 "Acrotriche depressa, commonly known as native currant or wiry ground-berry, is a dwarf evergreen perennial shrub native to southern Australia, occurring naturally in sandy or heavy clay moist soils. The fruits are eaten out-of-hand, or used in jams and jellies. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Acrotriche_depressa]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414957 <http://www.ars-grin.gov/cgi-bin/npgs/html/taxon.pl?1380>)
