# Class: obo:FOODON_03414962 (cinnamon rose plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414962 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414962 "Rosa majalis (cinnamon rose, double cinnamon rose) is a species of deciduous shrubs in the genus *Rosa*, native to forests of Europe and Siberia. It grows to 2 m. and yields edible hip fruits rich in vitamin C, which are used in medicine and to produce rose hip syrup. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosa_majalis]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414962 <http://eol.org/pages/231454>)
