# Class: obo:FOODON_03414977 (true cinnamon plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414977 obo:IAO_0000122)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414977 "Cinnamomum verum, called true cinnamon tree or Ceylon cinnamon tree is a small evergreen tree belonging to the family *Lauraceae*, native to Sri Lanka. Among other species, its inner bark is used to make cinnamon. The old botanical synonym for the tree-*Cinnamomum zeylanicum*-is derived from Sri Lanka's former name, Ceylon. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cinnamomum_verum]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414977 <http://eol.org/pages/490672>)
