# Class: obo:FOODON_03414978 (melientha plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03414978 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03414978 "Melientha is a genus of plants in the family *Opiliaceae* described as a genus in 1888. The genus contains only one known species, *Melientha suavis*, native to Southeast Asia. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Melientha] 
 The young shoots, leaves, inflorescences and young fruits are widely consumed as a vegetable after boiling. The ripe fruits are also edible (juicy mesocarp) and in Vietnam the seeds are eaten in the same way as groundnut after boiling or frying. [http://uses.plantnet-project.org/en/Melientha_suavis_(PROSEA)]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414978 <http://www.ars-grin.gov/cgi-bin/npgs/html/taxon.pl?405776>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03414978 langual:B4978)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym obo:FOODON_03414978 "Melientha suavis Pierre")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03414978 "melientha plant"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03414978 obo:FOODON_03411058)

