# Class: obo:FOODON_03415000 (muster john henry plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03415000 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03415000 "Tagetes minuta - muster John Henry, southern marigold, Khakibos , stinking roger, wild marigold, or black mint, is a tall upright marigold plant from the genus *Tagetes*, with small flowers, native to the southern half of South America. It is used as a culinary herb in Peru, Ecuador, and parts of Chile and Bolivia. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tagetes_minuta]"@en)
