AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03415002 "Tropaeolum, commonly known as nasturtium, is a genus of roughly 80 species of annual and perennial herbaceous flowering plants. The nasturtiums received their common name because they produce an oil similar to that of watercress (*Nasturtium officinale*). [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tropaeolum]"@en)
