# Class: obo:FOODON_03415036 (great pignut plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03415036 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03415036 "Bunium bulbocastanum is a plant species in the family *Apiaceae*. It is related to cumin (*Cuminum cyminum*) and commonly called black cumin, blackseed, black caraway, or great pignut, and has a smoky, earthy taste. It is often confused with *Nigella sativa* (which is also called black cumin, blackseed, and black caraway). [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bunium_bulbocastanum]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03415036 <http://eol.org/pages/581707>)
