# Class: obo:FOODON_03415049 (japanese quince plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03415049 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03415049 "Chaenomeles japonica, known as Maule's quince, is a species of flowering quince. The fruit is edible, but hard and astringent-tasting, unless bletted. The fruit is occasionally used in jam, jelly and pie making as a substitute for its cousin, the true quince, Cydonia oblonga. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chaenomeles_japonica]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03415049 <http://eol.org/pages/230570>)
