# Class: obo:FOODON_03415061 (chilean guava plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03415061 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03415061 "Ugni molinae, commonly known as Chilean guava, or strawberry myrtle, is a shrub native to Chile and adjacent regions of southern Argentina. The fruit is sometimes marketed as \"Ugniberry\", as \"New Zealand cranberry\" in New Zealand, and the name \"Tazziberry\" has been trademarked in Australia, but it is not a native plant to these countries. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ugni_molinae]"@en)
