AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03415063 "Maclura tricuspidata  is a tree native to East Asia, occasionally grown for its fruit, somewhat similar to that of the related mulberry (*Morus* spp.). It is also known by common names including cudrang, mandarin melon berry, silkworm thorn, zhe or che, and Chinese mulberry (but not to be confused with *Morus australis * also known by that name). [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maclura_tricuspidata]"@en)
