AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03415085 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03415085 "Angelica archangelica, commonly known as garden angelica, wild celery, and Norwegian angelica, is a biennial plant from the Apiaceae family, a subspecies of which is cultivated for its sweetly scented edible stems and roots. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Angelica_archangelica]"@en)
