# Class: obo:FOODON_03415146 (mullein plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03415146 "Verbascum, common name mullein (also known as velvet plant), is a genus of about 250 species of flowering plants in the figwort family *Scrophulariaceae*. They are native to Europe and Asia, with the highest species diversity in the Mediterranean. Mullein or \"mullein leaf\" often refers to the leaves of *Verbascum thapsus*, the great or common mullein, which is frequently used in herbal medicine.[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Verbascum]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03415146 <http://eol.org/pages/60976>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03415146 langual:B5146)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:FOODON_03415146 "Aaron's-rod")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:FOODON_03415146 "common mullein")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:FOODON_03415146 "flannel plant")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:FOODON_03415146 "velvet plant")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03415146 "mullein plant"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03415146 obo:FOODON_03413359)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03415146 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_39388))

# Class: obo:FOODON_03415147 (rockrose plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03415147 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03415147 "Cistus  is a genus of flowering plants in the rockrose family *Cistaceae*, containing about 20 species. In popular medicine, infusions of cistuses are used to treat diarrhea. *Cistus incanus* specifically is traditionally used for cold, flu, respiratory tract infections, etc. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cistus]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03415147 <http://eol.org/pages/38069>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03415147 langual:B5147)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03415147 "cistus"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:FOODON_03415147 "rock rose"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_03415147 "rockrose plant"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_03415147 obo:FOODON_03413359)

# Class: obo:FOODON_03415148 (silverweed plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03415148 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03415148 "Argentina anserina is a synonym of *Potentilla anserina* L., the accepted name of a perennial flowering plant in the rose family, *Rosaceae*. It is known by the common names \"silverweed\", common silverweed or silver cinquefoil. It was formerly believed to be useful for epilepsy, and that it could ward off witches and evil spirits. The plant has been cultivated as a food crop for its edible roots. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Argentina_anserina]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03415148 <http://eol.org/pages/301011>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03415148 <http://www.ars-grin.gov/cgi-bin/npgs/html/taxon.pl?29465>)
