# Class: obo:FOODON_03415155 (beebalm plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03415155 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03415155 "Monarda is a genus of flowering plants in the mint family, *Lamiaceae*. Common names include bee balm, horsemint, oswego tea, and bergamot, the latter inspired by the fragrance of the leaves. Several species, including Monarda fistulosa and M. didyma, have a long history of use as medicinal plants by many Native Americans. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monarda]"@en)
