# Class: obo:FOODON_03415171 (red sandalwood plant)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_03415171 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_03415171 "Pterocarpus santalinus, with the common names red sanders, red sandalwood, and saunderswood, is a species of *Pterocarpus* endemic to the southern Eastern Ghats mountain range of South India. The tree is not to be confused with the aromatic *Santalum* sandalwood trees that grow natively in South India. *Pterocarpus santalinus* is used in traditional herbal medicine [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pterocarpus_santalinus]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:FOODON_03415171 <http://eol.org/pages/643243>)
