AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:NCBITaxon_3712 "Brassica oleracea L.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym obo:NCBITaxon_3712 "Brassica oleracea L. var. conica DC.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:NCBITaxon_3712 "borecole"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:NCBITaxon_3712 "brassica oleracea convar. capitate  var. conica"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:NCBITaxon_3712 "\"It is considered to be closer to wild cabbage than most domesticated forms. The species *Brassica oleracea* contains a wide array of vegetables including broccoli, cauliflower, collard greens, and brussels sprouts. The cultivar group Acephala also includes spring greens and collard greens, which are extremely similar genetically.\" - Wikipedia"@en)

