# Class: obo:NCBITaxon_9913 (Bos taurus)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:NCBITaxon_9913 "Cattle (colloquially cows) are the most common type of large domesticated ungulates. They are a prominent modern member of the subfamily *Bovinae*, are the most widespread species of the genus *Bos*, and are most commonly classified collectively as *Bos taurus*... with three subspecies: *Bos taurus primigenius, Bos taurus indicus, Bos taurus taurus*."@en)
