# Class: obo:NCBITaxon_9938 (Ovis aries musimon)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:NCBITaxon_9938 obo:IAO_0000122)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:NCBITaxon_9938 "The mouflon (*Ovis aries orientalis* group) is a subspecies group of the wild sheep *Ovis aries*. Populations of *Ovis aries* can be partitioned into the mouflons (*orientalis* group) and urials or arkars (*vignei* group). The mouflon is thought to be one of the two ancestors for all modern domestic sheep breeds."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000118 obo:NCBITaxon_9938 "mouflon"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:NCBITaxon_9938 "WIKIPEDIA:Ovis_aries_orientalis")
