AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasSynonym obo:NCBITaxon_32201 "pecan nut"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:NCBITaxon_32201 "\"Pecan\" is from an Algonquian word, meaning a nut requiring a stone to crack. In Mexico, pecans and walnuts share the same Spanish name, nuez, which is a cognate of the English word nut.

LanguaL curation note: When indexing the pecan fruit (drupaceous nut) index both *PECAN [B1320]* and *FRUIT [C0167]* (or its more precidese narrower terms)."@en)
